DAY 26 - PART A: THEORY
StatefulSets: Stable Identity and Storage
Time: 40 minutes
==================================================================

1. WHY DEPLOYMENTS DON'T FIT DATABASES
--------------------------------------
Deployment pods are interchangeable: random names, start in any order,
all share ONE PVC (if any). A database cluster needs:
  - stable names (db-0 is the primary, db-1 a replica)
  - stable network identity (others connect to db-0 specifically)
  - its OWN disk per replica that follows it after rescheduling
  - ordered startup/shutdown


2. WHAT A STATEFULSET GUARANTEES
--------------------------------
  Stable names         web-0, web-1, web-2 (ordinal index)
  Stable DNS           web-0.web.default.svc.cluster.local
                       (needs a HEADLESS Service, field serviceName)
  Stable storage       volumeClaimTemplates -> one PVC per pod:
                       data-web-0, data-web-1 ... The PVC is NOT
                       deleted when the pod or the StatefulSet is
                       deleted (unless you set
                       persistentVolumeClaimRetentionPolicy).
  Ordered operations   create 0, then 1, then 2 (each Ready first);
                       delete in reverse; rolling update from highest
                       ordinal down.


3. YAML
-------
  apiVersion: apps/v1
  kind: StatefulSet
  metadata:
    name: web
  spec:
    serviceName: web          # headless Service name
    replicas: 3
    selector:
      matchLabels: {app: web}
    template:
      metadata:
        labels: {app: web}
      spec:
        containers:
        - name: nginx
          image: nginx:1.27
          volumeMounts:
          - name: data
            mountPath: /usr/share/nginx/html
    volumeClaimTemplates:
    - metadata:
        name: data
      spec:
        accessModes: ["ReadWriteOnce"]
        resources:
          requests:
            storage: 1Gi


4. OPTIONS
----------
podManagementPolicy: Parallel      start/stop all at once (no order)
updateStrategy:
  RollingUpdate  (default) with "partition: N" for canary: only pods
                 with ordinal >= N are updated
  OnDelete       update a pod only when you delete it


5. WHAT A STATEFULSET DOES NOT DO
---------------------------------
It doesn't know how to replicate your database, elect a primary, or
take backups. It gives identity + storage; the app (or an OPERATOR,
Week 9) does the clustering logic.

Production reality: most teams use MANAGED databases (RDS, Cloud SQL,
Azure Database) or a database operator (CloudNativePG, Percona,
Strimzi for Kafka) rather than hand-written StatefulSets.


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- StatefulSet = stable name + stable DNS + per-pod PVC + ordering.
- Needs a headless Service.
- PVCs survive pod and StatefulSet deletion.
